      "problem": "What is the cardinality of $Z\\times X$ for $Z={p,q,r}$ and $X={-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $Z$ and $X,$ the cardinality of $Z\\times X$ is\n\n$$\n|Z\\times X|=|Z|\\cdot |X|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|Z\\times X| & =|Z|\\cdot |X| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
